{
    "info": {
        "_postman_id": "99bba594-86e8-48d4-ab91-f433aef44a80",
        "name": "Nodefold API",
        "description": "# **Nodefold API**\n\nNodefold API is a RESTful API for managing design assets organized in folders. It allows authenticated users to create, organize and retrieve resources such as images, fonts, color palettes, icons and web links.\n\n**Base URL** `http://localhost/api`\n\n**Authentication** This API uses token based authentication via Laravel Passport. To access protected endpoints, include the token in the request header:\n\n`Authorization: Bearer {token}`\n\nThe token is obtained via `POST /login` and must be included in every subsequent request.\n\n**Response format** All responses are returned in JSON format.\n\n**Roles** The API handles two user roles:\n\n- `user` — standard access to their own folders and resources.\n    \n- `admin` — additional access to user management and global statistics.\n    \n\n### **HTTP Status codes**\n\n| **Code** | **Meaning** |\n| --- | --- |\n| **200** | Ok |\n| **201** | Created |\n| **204** | No Content |\n| **400** | Bad Request |\n| **401** | Unauthenticated |\n| **403** | Forbidden |\n| **404** | Not Faund |\n| **422** | Validation Error |",
        "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
        "_exporter_id": "53033314",
        "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/53033314-99bba594-86e8-48d4-ab91-f433aef44a80?source=collection_link"
    },
    "item": [
        {
            "name": "Auth",
            "item": [
                {
                    "name": "Register",
                    "event": [
                        {
                            "listen": "test",
                            "script": {
                                "exec": [
                                    "const response = pm.response.json();",
                                    "pm.environment.set(\"token\", response.token);"
                                ],
                                "type": "text/javascript",
                                "packages": {},
                                "requests": {}
                            }
                        }
                    ],
                    "request": {
                        "method": "POST",
                        "header": [],
                        "body": {
                            "mode": "raw",
                            "raw": "{\n    \"name\": \"TestName\",\n    \"email\": \"testUser@nodefold.com\",\n    \"password\": \"Password123\",\n    \"password_confirmation\": \"Password123\"\n}",
                            "options": {
                                "raw": {
                                    "language": "json"
                                }
                            }
                        },
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/register",
                            "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
                            "path": ["register"]
                        },
                        "description": "Creates a new user account by submitting the required registration details.\n\n**Endpoint:** `POST /api/v1/register`\n\n### Request Body\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `name` | string | The full name of the new user |\n| `email` | string | A valid and unique email address |\n| `password` | string | The desired account password |\n| `password_confirmation` | string | Must match the `password` field |\n\n### On Success\n\nReturns `201 Created` with the user data and a token.\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"user\": {\n    \"id\": 1,\n    \"name\": \"Test User\",\n    \"email\": \"demo@test.com\",\n    \"role\": \"user\"\n  },\n  \"token\": \"eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1...\"\n}\n\n ```\n\nThe token is automatically saved to the `token` environment variable and used to authenticate subsequent requests."
                    },
                    "response": []
                },
                {
                    "name": "Login",
                    "event": [
                        {
                            "listen": "test",
                            "script": {
                                "exec": [
                                    "const response = pm.response.json();",
                                    "pm.environment.set(\"token\", response.token);"
                                ],
                                "type": "text/javascript",
                                "packages": {},
                                "requests": {}
                            }
                        },
                        {
                            "listen": "prerequest",
                            "script": {
                                "exec": [""],
                                "type": "text/javascript",
                                "packages": {},
                                "requests": {}
                            }
                        }
                    ],
                    "request": {
                        "method": "POST",
                        "header": [],
                        "body": {
                            "mode": "raw",
                            "raw": "{\n    \"email\": \"testUser@nodefold.com\",\n    \"password\": \"Password123\"\n}",
                            "options": {
                                "raw": {
                                    "language": "json"
                                }
                            }
                        },
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/login",
                            "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
                            "path": ["login"]
                        },
                        "description": "Authenticates an existing user and returns an access token.\n\n**Endpoint:** `POST /api/v1/login`\n\n### Request Body\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `email` | string | The registered email address |\n| `password` | string | The account password |\n\n### On Success\n\nReturns `200 OK` with the user data and a token.\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"user\": {\n    \"id\": 1,\n    \"name\": \"Test User\",\n    \"email\": \"demo@test.com\",\n    \"role\": \"user\"\n  },\n  \"token\": \"eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1...\"\n}\n\n ```\n\nThe token is automatically saved to the `token` environment variable and used to authenticate subsequent requests."
                    },
                    "response": []
                },
                {
                    "name": "Logout",
                    "request": {
                        "auth": {
                            "type": "bearer",
                            "bearer": [
                                {
                                    "key": "token",
                                    "value": "{{token}}",
                                    "type": "string"
                                }
                            ]
                        },
                        "method": "POST",
                        "header": [],
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/logout",
                            "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
                            "path": ["logout"]
                        },
                        "description": "Invalidates the current access token and logs the user out.\n\n**Endpoint:** `POST /api/v1/logout`\n\n### Authentication\n\nRequires a valid Bearer token in the `Authorization` header.\n\n### On Success\n\nReturns `200 OK` with a confirmation message.\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"message\": \"Logged out successfully\"\n}\n\n ```\n\nThe token is invalidated server-side and must be discarded by the client."
                    },
                    "response": []
                }
            ],
            "description": "Endpoints for user registration, login and logout.\n\nRegistration and login do not require authentication. Every other endpoint in this API requires a **valid Bearer token** obtained from `POST /login`.\n\nUpon login, a token is returned that must be stored by the client and included in the `Authorization` header of every subsequent request. Upon logout, the token is invalidated server-side and must be discarded by the client."
        },
