            "description": "Endpoints for managing the creation user's resources.\n\n##### All endpoints in this section **require a valid Bearer token** in the `Authorization` header.\n\nA user can view their resources, update their information, manage tags and delete the resources.\n\n### Resources allowed\n\n| Resource | Source | Info |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `Images` | Upload from URL or device | jpg, jpeg, png, webp, gif — max 10MB |\n| `Fonts` | Upload from URL | Use of [https://fonts.google.com/](https://fonts.google.com/) is recommended |\n| `Webs` | Upload from URL | No URL restriction |\n| `Color Palettes` | Upload from URL | It's required to use [https://coolors.co](https://coolors.co) |\n| `Icons` | Upload from URL | No URL restriction |\n\n### Note\n\nIn order to upload resources, the user must first create a folder.\n\n### color_data field\n\nThe `color_data` field is only populated for `color_palette` type resources. It contains an array of hex color codes automatically extracted from a Coolors.co URL. Example: `[\"dad7cd\", \"a3b18a\", \"588157\", \"3a5a40\", \"344e41\"]` For all other resource types, `color_data`will be `null`."
